Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `trip_seconds`: trip duration in seconds ⇒ convert to minutes, build quantiles, filter 0–60 min  
• `fare`: cost of the trip ⇒ aggregate (AVG) inside each quantile group  
• `unique_key`: trip identifier ⇒ COUNT(*) of trips  
• `trip_start_timestamp` (optional) ⇒ no direct need, but can be used for time‑range samples in exploratory steps  

Main condition that will be needed  
```sql
WHERE trip_seconds > 0                             -- positive durations only
  AND trip_seconds <= 60*60                        -- 0‑60 minutes (≤3600 s)
```

Below are ten different BigQuery SQL queries that progress from very simple exploration to the complete answer.  
(Replace nothing – the identifiers already contain the real project, dataset, and table names.)

```sql
-- 1) Preview a few trips with their raw duration and fare
SELECT unique_key,
       trip_seconds,
       fare
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) See distinct payment types just to get a sense of the data
SELECT DISTINCT payment_type
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Convert seconds to rounded minutes and look at the distribution (sample)
SELECT ROUND(trip_seconds / 60.0) AS trip_minutes
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
WHERE  trip_seconds BETWEEN 1 AND 3600
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Quick stats: min / max / avg duration (minutes) for trips 0‑60 min
SELECT MIN(trip_seconds) / 60     AS min_minutes,
       MAX(trip_seconds) / 60     AS max_minutes,
       AVG(trip_seconds) / 60     AS avg_minutes
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
WHERE  trip_seconds BETWEEN 1 AND 3600;
```

```sql
-- 5) Distinct companies that had trips lasting ≤10 minutes
SELECT DISTINCT company
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
WHERE  trip_seconds BETWEEN 1 AND 600
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Sample 20 trips showing rounded minutes, fare, and company
SELECT unique_key,
       ROUND(trip_seconds/60.0) AS trip_minutes,
       fare,
       company
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
WHERE  trip_seconds BETWEEN 1 AND 3600
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Use NTILE(6) to assign each trip to one of six equal‑frequency buckets
SELECT unique_key,
       ROUND(trip_seconds/60.0) AS trip_minutes,
       NTILE(6) OVER (ORDER BY trip_seconds) AS duration_bucket
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
WHERE  trip_seconds BETWEEN 1 AND 3600
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) For a quick check, count trips in each bucket (0‑60 min only)
SELECT duration_bucket,
       COUNT(*) AS trips_in_bucket
FROM  (
        SELECT NTILE(6) OVER (ORDER BY trip_seconds) AS duration_bucket
        FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
        WHERE  trip_seconds BETWEEN 1 AND 3600
      )
GROUP BY duration_bucket
ORDER BY duration_bucket;
```

```sql
-- 9) Show min / max rounded minutes for each bucket (sanity check)
SELECT duration_bucket,
       MIN(ROUND(trip_seconds/60.0)) AS min_minutes,
       MAX(ROUND(trip_seconds/60.0)) AS max_minutes
FROM  (
        SELECT trip_seconds,
               NTILE(6) OVER (ORDER BY trip_seconds) AS duration_bucket
        FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
        WHERE  trip_seconds BETWEEN 1 AND 3600
      )
GROUP BY duration_bucket
ORDER BY duration_bucket;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final answer: min & max trip duration (rounded minutes),
--     total trips, and average fare for each of the six quantile groups
SELECT duration_bucket                             AS quantile_group,
       MIN(ROUND(trip_seconds/60.0)) AS min_minutes,
       MAX(ROUND(trip_seconds/60.0)) AS max_minutes,
       COUNT(*)                       AS total_trips,
       ROUND(AVG(fare), 2)            AS avg_fare
FROM  (
        SELECT trip_seconds,
               fare,
               NTILE(6) OVER (ORDER BY trip_seconds) AS duration_bucket
        FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
        WHERE  trip_seconds BETWEEN 1 AND 3600
      )
GROUP BY duration_bucket
ORDER BY duration_bucket;
```
